(BAS-45 - WITHDRAWN 2026-10-17: the hang example this row cited (manual
 lines 186 to 199 at vox a0a2ecc) was removed when vox #289 re-told the
 paragraph rules. The behaviour it showed still follows from rule 2,
 LANGUAGE.md:167: the blank line ends the While, so `increment counter` is
 a statement after the loop, the condition never changes and the loop
 never ends, and `Print "end"` never runs.
 The old manual copy printed `inner 1` / `inner 2` forever; this retained
 copy replaces that print with a silent assignment so the hang can be
 recorded as a bounded timeout instead of unbounded output.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-45.vox -o p && timeout 10 ./p
 expected output:
